# The Content-Security-Policy in index.html admits its inline boot script by a
# SHA-256 of that script's exact bytes, and tests/themeboot.test.ts recomputes
# the hash from the file on disk to prove the two still agree.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true -- the default on a Windows checkout -- the working
# tree gets CRLF, so the recomputed hash is of different bytes than the ones
# hashed when the policy was written. The test then fails on Windows and passes
# in CI on Linux, which is the worst of both: it cannot be trusted locally, and
# a `npm run build` on Windows emits a document whose policy blocks its own
# boot script.
#
# Pinned so that the working tree, the object store, CI and the browser are all
# hashing the same bytes.
index.html text eol=lf
app/index.html text eol=lf
